1
00:00:20.506 --> 00:00:27.506
Invoices are the bill. The money itself
lives on the Income page. They're linked.

2
00:00:27.535 --> 00:00:30.035
Rent arrived? Mark the invoice paid…

3
00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:58.608
…and the income entry writes itself. Same
amount, same tenant, same month.

4
00:01:01.138 --> 00:01:05.138
It works the other way too. Record the
payment as income first…

5
00:01:13.255 --> 00:01:19.255
…and the open invoice for that month flips
to paid on its own.

6
00:01:19.257 --> 00:01:25.257
One action, both sides. Enter it twice and
you'd be double-counting — so don't.

7
00:01:27.641 --> 00:01:34.141
Month-end: select many invoices at once.
Email every PDF, or mark them all paid.

8
00:01:38.068 --> 00:01:43.568
Each one gets its income entry, exactly
like the single click.

9
00:01:44.756 --> 00:01:49.756
Mistakes happen. On a paid invoice there's
exactly one way back: Revert to unpaid.

10
00:01:53.658 --> 00:01:59.214
It reopens the invoice and deletes the
linked income entry too — books stay

11
00:01:59.214 --> 00:02:00.714
clean.

12
00:02:00.714 --> 00:02:05.187
Bill with invoices, receive with income,
and let the link do the bookkeeping.

13
00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:09.191
Next: what happens when the tenant says
'I've paid' — verifying proof of payment.
